  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466446",
      "title": "Adding Auto-Logout",
      "lectureOrder": 630,
      "videoOrder": 581,
      "sourceHash": "4ca5d3e2368239e8c67034e1732deb65e4a100c57ad9854fcacd4fa1ab421723",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.37,
          "end": 4.752,
          "en": "Presenter: Having the autoLogin in place is great,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.752,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "but what about a autoLogout?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 9.66,
          "en": "Because our token will expire,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.66,
          "end": 13.05,
          "en": "it has an expiry time of one hour, once we get it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.05,
          "end": 15.81,
          "en": "And therefore, right now, we have a bug in the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.81,
          "end": 18.96,
          "en": "because this token will never expire,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.96,
          "end": 20.46,
          "en": "or the token will expire,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.46,
          "end": 22.913,
          "en": "but our application won't reflect that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.913,
          "end": 25.83,
          "en": "We'll automatically log the user in forever,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.83,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "because we now have that snapshot here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "and we never clear that snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 31.68,
          "en": "And, sure, we could clear it when we log out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.68,
          "end": 33.99,
          "en": "and we should do that, and we will do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 36.15,
          "en": "but it will never clear automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.15,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "If the token expired after one hour,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 39.81,
          "en": "nothing changes in our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 42.182,
          "en": "And that, of course, is something we have to change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 42.182,
          "end": 45.18,
          "en": "So first of all, in the auth service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 45.18,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "we should make sure that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 48.918,
          "en": "since we store a snapshot upon logging in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 48.918,
          "end": 52.44,
          "en": "we also clear that snapshot here in the logout function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 52.44,
          "end": 53.64,
          "en": "because if a user logs out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 53.64,
          "end": 56.52,
          "en": "we certainly have to clear everything about that user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 56.52,
          "end": 57.6,
          "en": "in our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 57.6,
          "end": 59.73,
          "en": "And that includes the local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 59.73,
          "end": 61.55,
          "en": "So, here, we should take our local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 61.55,
          "end": 63.153999999999996,
          "en": "and we can simply call clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 63.153999999999996,
          "end": 65.554,
          "en": "to clear all the data in the local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 65.554,
          "end": 67.458,
          "en": "That, however, only makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 67.458,
          "end": 69.72,
          "en": "if we have no other data in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 69.72,
          "end": 71.7,
          "en": "If we do have, then we clear that as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 71.7,
          "end": 73.97,
          "en": "So, it's better if we don't clear all the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 73.97,
          "end": 76.53,
          "en": "but instead if we call remove item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 76.53,
          "end": 79.17,
          "en": "and we just remove that user data key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 79.17,
          "end": 80.81,
          "en": "and the data that's stored there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 80.81,
          "end": 83.989,
          "en": "Now, that's step number one that we do actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 83.989,
          "end": 86.91,
          "en": "clear the data when we log out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 86.91,
          "end": 88.816,
          "en": "But now, we also need to set a timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 88.816,
          "end": 93.589,
          "en": "when the token is stored, or when we first get a token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 93.589,
          "end": 96.63,
          "en": "so that we know when to invalidate that token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 96.63,
          "end": 98.194,
          "en": "at a later point of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 98.194,
          "end": 102.18,
          "en": "And for this, I'll add yet another method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 102.18,
          "end": 104.4,
          "en": "which I'll call autoLogout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 104.4,
          "end": 107.78999999999999,
          "en": "We have autoLogin for automatically retrieving user data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 107.78999999999999,
          "end": 108.99000000000001,
          "en": "and logging the user in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 108.99000000000001,
          "end": 111.6,
          "en": "Now we need a method that sets a timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 111.6,
          "end": 114.839,
          "en": "and manages a timer for automatically logging the user out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 114.839,
          "end": 119.839,
          "en": "AutoLogout should get the expirationDuration here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 121.35,
          "end": 123.3,
          "en": "which is a number, as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 123.3,
          "end": 126.6,
          "en": "So, this will be the amount of milliseconds we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 126.6,
          "end": 128.52,
          "en": "until the token is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 128.52,
          "end": 130.62,
          "en": "Let's say, of course, you could write this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 130.62,
          "end": 133.02,
          "en": "in a different logic, but I will go with milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 133.02,
          "end": 134.668,
          "en": "which we get as an argument here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 134.668,
          "end": 137.34,
          "en": "and then we can use setTimeout in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 137.34,
          "end": 141.688,
          "en": "to set that to that duration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 141.688,
          "end": 146.688,
          "en": "And after that duration here, I want to call this logout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 147.61599999999999,
          "end": 148.92000000000002,
          "en": "So the logout function we have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 148.92000000000002,
          "end": 150.57,
          "en": "should be called automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 150.57,
          "end": 152.788,
          "en": "after our expirationDuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 152.788,
          "end": 156.09,
          "en": "Now, the important thing is that when we do log out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 156.09,
          "end": 159.45,
          "en": "we clear that timer, because if we log out automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 159.45,
          "end": 160.59,
          "en": "then it's no problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 160.59,
          "end": 161.848,
          "en": "Then the timer expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 161.848,
          "end": 164.892,
          "en": "But if we log out manually, because this button is pressed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 164.892,
          "end": 167.7,
          "en": "we auto-call logout, and then we still have the timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 167.7,
          "end": 170.52,
          "en": "in the background, which calls logout again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 170.52,
          "end": 172.02,
          "en": "at a later point of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 172.02,
          "end": 173.55,
          "en": "Now, we don't want to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 173.55,
          "end": 175.23,
          "en": "If a user logs out on his own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 175.23,
          "end": 177.69,
          "en": "then the current session, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 177.69,
          "end": 180.33,
          "en": "the current lifetime of the token we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 180.33,
          "end": 182.55,
          "en": "ends anyways, and therefore we should also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 182.55,
          "end": 185.891,
          "en": "clear that token expiration timer when we log out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 185.891,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "Now, clearing that timer is not too hard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 191.37,
          "en": "We simply store it in our property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 191.37,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "which we can name tokenExpirationTimer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 195.6,
          "en": "but you can name this however you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 195.6,
          "end": 199.173,
          "en": "and that this will actually be, I'll type any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 200.57999999999998,
          "end": 203.49,
          "en": "And now let's store our timer down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 203.49,
          "end": 206.73,
          "en": "SetTimeout returns a reference to that timer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 206.73,
          "end": 209.756,
          "en": "so we can simply store that in tokenExpirationTimer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 209.756,
          "end": 211.62,
          "en": "And in the logout function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 211.62,
          "end": 213.66,
          "en": "we now just have to clear that timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 213.66,
          "end": 217.32,
          "en": "So in there, in logout, we should check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 217.32,
          "end": 220.165,
          "en": "if we do have an active timer, because maybe we don't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 220.165,
          "end": 223.315,
          "en": "Maybe it expired anyways, then we can't clear it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 223.315,
          "end": 226.763,
          "en": "But if we do have an active one, so if this is true-ish,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 226.763,
          "end": 230.59300000000002,
          "en": "then we should clear our Timeout here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 230.59300000000002,
          "end": 234.06,
          "en": "and set this tokenExpriationTimer or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 234.06,
          "end": 237.42000000000002,
          "en": "past this tokenExpirationTimer, into clearTimeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 237.42000000000002,
          "end": 240.84,
          "en": "And this will, well, clear the tokenEpirationTimer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 240.84,
          "end": 243.15,
          "en": "and thereafter reset tokenExpirationTimer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 243.15,
          "end": 244.753,
          "en": "back to null manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 244.753,
          "end": 247.585,
          "en": "So now, we clear the timer when we log out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 247.585,
          "end": 251.79,
          "en": "and we also set it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 251.79,
          "end": 253.38,
          "en": "Now, of course, we just have to make sure we do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 253.38,
          "end": 256.437,
          "en": "call autoLogout, because currently we are doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 256.437,
          "end": 259.2,
          "en": "and we need to call autoLogout to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 259.2,
          "end": 261.33,
          "en": "that this timer actually starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 261.33,
          "end": 263.816,
          "en": "Now, where do we need to call that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 263.816,
          "end": 267.99,
          "en": "Basically, whenever we admit a new user to our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 267.99,
          "end": 270.06,
          "en": "So whenever we use our user subject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 270.06,
          "end": 271.47,
          "en": "And that would be the case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 271.47,
          "end": 275.113,
          "en": "in handleAuthentication, and also in autoLogin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 275.113,
          "end": 277.769,
          "en": "Now let's start with handleAuthentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 277.769,
          "end": 281.561,
          "en": "There we do admit our user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 281.561,
          "end": 283.86,
          "en": "Now, right after doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 283.86,
          "end": 285.611,
          "en": "or right before doing that, doesn't matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 285.611,
          "end": 288,
          "en": "we should call autoLogout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 288,
          "end": 290.01,
          "en": "and pass our current expiration time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 290.01,
          "end": 292.71,
          "en": "into that autoLogout function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 292.71,
          "end": 295.181,
          "en": "Now, the current expiration time, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 295.181,
          "end": 298.601,
          "en": "is our expiresIn value here, which is in seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 298.601,
          "end": 300.87,
          "en": "times 1000,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 300.87,
          "end": 303.66,
          "en": "because we expect milliseconds in autoLogout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 303.66,
          "end": 305.58,
          "en": "Since expiresIn is in seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 305.58,
          "end": 308.283,
          "en": "times 1000 gives us the amount in milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 309.45,
          "end": 311.52,
          "en": "Now that's handle authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 311.52,
          "end": 315.21,
          "en": "In autoLogin, it's a tiny bit more complex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 315.21,
          "end": 317.64,
          "en": "Here, when we know that we do have a token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 317.64,
          "end": 320.293,
          "en": "and we therefore admit our user to the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 320.293,
          "end": 324.793,
          "en": "There, we also want to call this autoLogout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 324.793,
          "end": 328.842,
          "en": "But here, we now have to calculate the remaining time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 328.842,
          "end": 331.661,
          "en": "We do have our token expiration date, after all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 331.661,
          "end": 333.6,
          "en": "And, of course, we can always find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 333.6,
          "end": 335.4,
          "en": "what the current date is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 335.4,
          "end": 340.4,
          "en": "So our expirationDuration is basically this timestamp here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 343.38,
          "end": 346.38,
          "en": "So the token expiration date wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 346.38,
          "end": 348.3,
          "en": "into a date in milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 348.3,
          "end": 350.053,
          "en": "which we get by calling getTime,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 350.053,
          "end": 352.44,
          "en": "minus the current timestamp,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 352.44,
          "end": 356.34000000000003,
          "en": "which we get with new Date in milliseconds with getTime.",
          "zh": ""
